# Normalize text line endings to LF in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The test suite asserts on the *text* of stylesheets and
# on serialized project JSON, so a CRLF checkout can change test outcomes even
# when no code changed. `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows was enough to fail
# three assertions on line endings alone.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect text vs binary per file; `eol=lf` then pins the
# working-tree form so a developer's platform cannot change what CI sees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated bundles and lockfiles are compared byte-for-byte in places, so keep
# them out of end-of-line conversion entirely.
package-lock.json -text

# Binary assets. Never diffed, never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.aab binary
*.apk binary
*.ipa binary
